After including the AIClient script, you can create an instance and generate text or images:

```javascript
const client = new AIClient();
client.setApiKey('YOUR_API_KEY');

// Generate a text response
client.setType('text');
const response = await client.generate('Hello AI!');
console.log(response);

// Generate an image
client.setType('image');
const imageBlob = await client.generate('A futuristic city at sunset');
```

The `generate` method returns a string for text or a Blob for images.

```javascript
const client = new AIClient();
client.setApiKey('YOUR_API_KEY');
client.setType('text');
const response = await client.generate('Write a short story about a robot.');
console.log(response);
```

```javascript
const client = new AIClient();
client.setApiKey('YOUR_API_KEY');
client.setType('image');
const imageBlob = await client.generate('A cyberpunk cityscape at night');
// You can create a URL to display the image
const url = URL.createObjectURL(imageBlob);
document.querySelector('#output-image').src = url;
```
